    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "https://www.auctioneera.ie/property/73-coultry-avenue-ballymun-ballymun-dublin-d09-y771\r\nImportant note: Details of upcoming viewings and latest offers are available at the Auctioneera website link above.\r\n\r\nAuctioneera is delighted to present 73 Coultry Avenue, Ballymun.\r\n\r\nSituated in the mature residential area of Ballymun, this is a delightful end-of-terrace property offering significant potential in a prime Dublin location. From the exterior, the property presents a classic architectural style with its brick façade and pitched roof. The presence of a generous grassy lawn at the front, complemented by a hedge boundary, provides an inviting entrance. The property boasts a substantial garden to the side and rear, accessible through a separate side entrance, ideal for further landscaping or potential development.\r\n\r\nUpon entering the property, the ground floor welcomes you with a spacious living room, characterised by large windows that invite abundant natural light. The room’s layout allows for versatile arrangements to accommodate various furnishing styles. The floor plan reveals direct access to the kitchen, which appears functional and allows for some updating to enhance its utility and style. Adjacent to the kitchen, large doors lead to the garden, making it perfect for indoor-outdoor living.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the accommodation comprises four well-appointed bedrooms. Each room is sizeable, providing ample space for storage and personalisation to fit family needs. The bathroom facilities are conveniently located for shared access.\r\n\r\nThe property's location is hard to beat, with LIDL and a bus stop to the city centre and airport just a short walk away, ensuring excellent connectivity and convenience. Surrounded by local schools, sports clubs, and other amenities, this home is exceptionally situated for family living or attracting long-term tenants as an investment.\r\n\r\nWith its extensive garden space and potential for expansion, this property is perfect for growing families, first-time buyers looking for a robust long-term investment, or investors keen on tapping into Dublin's vibrant rental market. The potential for enhancement through double-height extensions or additional garden cabins, as seen in neighbouring properties, further adds to its appeal."
      },
